WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.234
-Welcome back
to the show.

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:03.467
-Thank you.
-They love you. We love you.

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:04.801
-Thanks for having me.

00:00:04.801 --> 00:00:06.300
-No, I'm so psyched
that you're here.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:08.834
I can't wait to talk about
all things "Funny Girl."

00:00:08.834 --> 00:00:11.167
And also, the new cast recording
of the album.

00:00:11.167 --> 00:00:13.334
I want to hear everything.
But first,

00:00:13.334 --> 00:00:14.934
today's Friday the 13th.

00:00:14.934 --> 00:00:16.667
And I was saying backstage,
I go,

00:00:16.667 --> 00:00:18.434
"Are you superstitious at all?"

00:00:18.434 --> 00:00:20.200
And boy, was I surprised
you're very superstitious.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:21.734
-I'm a little too
superstitious.

00:00:21.734 --> 00:00:23.200
And it's funny,
because I actually didn't know

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.734
it was Friday the 13th
until I heard you say that.

00:00:25.734 --> 00:00:27.534
-Yeah.
-So now, I'm like, "Oh, my God,

00:00:27.534 --> 00:00:28.634
what do I have to do?"

00:00:28.634 --> 00:00:31.367
-No.
But how superstitious are you?

00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:33.934
-You know, it's interesting.
I know I am,

00:00:33.934 --> 00:00:36.033
but I realized it --
the other night,

00:00:36.033 --> 00:00:37.667
I went out with Jonathan Grough,
our friend,

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:38.767
and our other friend --
[ Audience cheers ]

00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:40.133
I know.
-Yeah, we love him.

00:00:40.133 --> 00:00:42.000
-And our other friend,
John Gallagher, who we were all

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.300
in "Spring Awakening" together.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:44.534
And they were like, "Why are
you carrying around this,

00:00:44.534 --> 00:00:46.567
like, extremely large bag?"

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:51.067
And I realized that 90% of it is
just like weird good luck charms

00:00:51.067 --> 00:00:52.767
and things that I have
to lug around with me.

00:00:52.767 --> 00:00:54.167
-Like what? What type of things?

00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:56.100
-I have, like, a race car
of my son's in there.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:59.434
I have a Christmas ornament
that my mom gave me. [ Laughs ]

00:00:59.434 --> 00:01:01.000
-Really?
-But it was -- you know,

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.601
when I did "Spring Awakening,"
a lot of the superstitions got,

00:01:03.601 --> 00:01:05.033
like, a little over the top.

00:01:05.033 --> 00:01:08.067
Jonathan and I ran through
every line from the entire show

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:10.167
every single day
before the show.

00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:12.801
We had to read from this,
like, quote book

00:01:12.801 --> 00:01:15.067
that you would buy at, like,
a Barnes &amp; Noble called

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:16.434
"I Hope You Dance."

00:01:16.434 --> 00:01:19.033
And we would have to pick, like,
a quote from it to read

00:01:19.033 --> 00:01:20.133
every night.

00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:22.801
So, now at "Funny Girl,"
I do less.

00:01:22.801 --> 00:01:25.834
I just carry the things with me,
but I don't do anything.

00:01:25.834 --> 00:01:27.000
-Good, okay.
Good, all right.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.734
-But New Year's,
I'm also very superstitious.

00:01:29.734 --> 00:01:31.067
-What do you do
on New Years?

00:01:31.067 --> 00:01:33.567
-I've got to do 12 grapes.
Do people know about this?

00:01:33.567 --> 00:01:34.701
[ Audience cheers ]
Okay.

00:01:34.701 --> 00:01:36.000
-Wait, I didn't know about this.
[ Man cheering ]

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.501
-Whoo!

00:01:37.501 --> 00:01:38.834
-What's 12 grapes?

00:01:38.834 --> 00:01:41.834
-12 grapes -- there's like --
I don't even know why.

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:43.801
It's, like, for good fortune.

00:01:43.801 --> 00:01:45.467
And, like, they have to be
green.

00:01:45.467 --> 00:01:47.000
I wear, like, certain colors

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.501
and I listen
to certain music, so --

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:50.567
-Wowzers.
-Yeah.

00:01:50.567 --> 00:01:51.934
-I mean, I did a little bit.

00:01:51.934 --> 00:01:54.300
But I was never got that --
the more I think about it,

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.667
I used to cut a birthday cake

00:01:55.667 --> 00:01:57.400
and wish I was on
"Saturday Night Live."

00:01:57.400 --> 00:01:59.667
[ Audience laughs ]
For real.

00:01:59.667 --> 00:02:01.667
And if I threw a coin
in a fountain,

00:02:01.667 --> 00:02:02.734
I'd wish I was on
"Saturday Night Live."

00:02:02.734 --> 00:02:03.767
And I really did.
-There you go.

00:02:03.767 --> 00:02:04.767
And then it worked out.

00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:06.701
-Maybe we manifested it.
-Yeah!

00:02:06.701 --> 00:02:08.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:10.267
Aww.

00:02:10.267 --> 00:02:11.734
-Congrats on "Funny Girl,"
by the way.

00:02:11.734 --> 00:02:13.801
-Thank you.
-It is breaking records.

00:02:13.801 --> 00:02:15.067
It is shattering records.

00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:17.400
It set the August Wilson
Theater's box office record

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.801
last month, and then you beat it
again two weeks later.

00:02:19.801 --> 00:02:21.000
-Yeah, I heard.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:22.133 --> 00:02:23.567
-I mean, crushed it.

00:02:23.567 --> 00:02:25.934
-Thank you.
And we're having a lot of fun,

00:02:25.934 --> 00:02:27.000
too, which is really important.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:28.300
-But you're just nailing
everything.

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.033
By the way, you were amazing
at the parade as well.

00:02:30.033 --> 00:02:31.167
-Thank you so much.
-You were great here.

00:02:31.167 --> 00:02:32.467
You performed live.
But just all this stuff.

00:02:32.467 --> 00:02:33.901
It's a lot of pressure.
-Thank you.

00:02:33.901 --> 00:02:35.701
I read somewhere that
Barbra Streisand

00:02:35.701 --> 00:02:37.834
sent you a letter.
-Yes.

00:02:37.834 --> 00:02:39.968
-The one and only
Barbra Streisand, who we love,

00:02:39.968 --> 00:02:42.234
you got a letter,
and she said, "Thumbs up."

00:02:42.234 --> 00:02:44.467
-She did. She gave me
the thumbs up, which I was so --

00:02:44.467 --> 00:02:45.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:45.634 --> 00:02:47.000
Thank you!

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.701
-Did you freak out?
-I did. I cried.

00:02:49.701 --> 00:02:50.868
-Of course, you had to.
-I cried.

00:02:50.868 --> 00:02:52.701
I filmed myself opening it.

00:02:52.701 --> 00:02:55.234
It was like, literally,
it was like a gold envelope.

00:02:55.234 --> 00:02:56.901
It flew in on doves.

00:02:56.901 --> 00:02:57.901
Like, you know.

00:02:57.901 --> 00:02:58.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.901 --> 00:03:00.267
-As Barbra would.

00:03:00.267 --> 00:03:01.634
-It came in through my window
of my dressing room.

00:03:01.634 --> 00:03:02.667
-That's what she does,
of course.

00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:04.567
The cartoon birds.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:03:04.567 --> 00:03:06.601
It was so incredible.

00:03:06.601 --> 00:03:08.834
And now it's like, I --
everyone's like,

00:03:08.834 --> 00:03:09.901
"Are you going to frame it?

00:03:09.901 --> 00:03:11.634
Like, what are you going to do
with it?"

00:03:11.634 --> 00:03:12.834
-You have to frame it.

00:03:12.834 --> 00:03:15.200
-I actually just -- I put it in
my safe at home.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:16.901
-Yeah.
-And the only thing I have

00:03:16.901 --> 00:03:19.300
in my safe is a letter
from Barbra Streisand

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:20.367
and my son's -- the hair --

00:03:20.367 --> 00:03:22.934
the first hair we cut
from his haircut.

00:03:22.934 --> 00:03:24.667
-That's perfect to me.
That sounds like exactly --

00:03:24.667 --> 00:03:26.067
-So, it's my son's hair
and a letter

00:03:26.067 --> 00:03:27.901
from Barbra Streisand.
[ Laughs ]

00:03:27.901 --> 00:03:30.133
-That's the best.
-That's where it's gonna stay.

00:03:30.133 --> 00:03:32.200
-Now, do you respond
to Barbra Streisand?

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:36.234
-I was able to get a message
to her through a friend

00:03:36.234 --> 00:03:38.334
to tell her thank you so much.

00:03:38.334 --> 00:03:39.534
But like, I don't know.

00:03:39.534 --> 00:03:41.334
Like, maybe I could, like,
direct message her

00:03:41.334 --> 00:03:42.667
on, like, Instagram
or something.

00:03:42.667 --> 00:03:44.634
-I don't know. I mean, with
Barbra, I don't know.

00:03:44.634 --> 00:03:46.534
-Barbra, I know you're
watching this right now.

00:03:46.534 --> 00:03:47.667
Thank you so much.

00:03:47.667 --> 00:03:49.033
-Yeah, we love you.

00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:50.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:50.334 --> 00:03:51.734
She's the coolest.
-Yes.

00:03:51.734 --> 00:03:55.534
-What would you -- what will you
do if she comes to see the show?

00:03:55.534 --> 00:03:56.801
Will you freak out?

00:03:56.801 --> 00:03:57.934
Would you want to know
that she's there?

00:03:57.934 --> 00:03:59.367
-I'll die. I'll black out.

00:03:59.367 --> 00:04:00.801
[ Laughter ]

00:04:00.801 --> 00:04:02.100
-I mean, would you want to know
if she's in the audience?

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.701
-It's funny, this is
the first show I've ever done

00:04:04.701 --> 00:04:06.834
where I love knowing
that people are there.

00:04:06.834 --> 00:04:08.434
It's super interactive.

00:04:08.434 --> 00:04:10.801
It's such a fun show.

00:04:10.801 --> 00:04:12.801
You know, Jarod, when he does
his tap during the show,

00:04:12.801 --> 00:04:16.367
we talk to the audience,
and it's a great back and forth.

00:04:16.367 --> 00:04:18.200
So, I love it.
-Do you act differently

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:20.300
depending on who -- if you
recognize somebody

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:22.667
in the audience?
-I would say 99% no.

00:04:22.667 --> 00:04:24.567
But Chris Rock was there
the other night,

00:04:24.567 --> 00:04:27.100
and I was like,
"I need to be funny."

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:29.000
And I just -- I have to be.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:31.634
I know I need to be funny every
night, but I was like,

00:04:31.634 --> 00:04:34.234
I just want Chris Rock
to tell me that I was funny.

00:04:34.234 --> 00:04:35.901
Like that was --
-Yeah, of course.

00:04:35.901 --> 00:04:37.734
-But if Barbra were there,
I would --

00:04:37.734 --> 00:04:40.834
The other night I saw a woman
that I thought was her,

00:04:40.834 --> 00:04:43.234
and I felt like
my mouth got dry,

00:04:43.234 --> 00:04:45.234
and it was like I just, like,

00:04:45.234 --> 00:04:46.767
started hearing ringing
in my ears.

00:04:46.767 --> 00:04:49.200
-I will go -- Barbra,
if you need a date,

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:51.234
I'm with you, bud. Let's go.
Let's go check this out.

00:04:51.234 --> 00:04:53.601
-That would make me feel
better, if you were with her.

00:04:53.601 --> 00:04:54.834
-It would? I would go.
-It would make me feel better.

00:04:54.834 --> 00:04:56.601
-She's a blast.

00:04:56.601 --> 00:04:58.067
Can we talk about
the new cast album?

00:04:58.067 --> 00:04:59.734
-Yeah.
-Congrats on this.

00:04:59.734 --> 00:05:00.868
-Thank you.

00:05:00.868 --> 00:05:02.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:02.033 --> 00:05:05.033
-The new cast recording
of "Funny Girl."

00:05:05.033 --> 00:05:06.901
This came out right around
the holidays.

00:05:06.901 --> 00:05:08.400
-It did.
You know, it was so wild.

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:09.701
We recorded it.

00:05:09.701 --> 00:05:12.234
I literally finished a show
on a Sunday

00:05:12.234 --> 00:05:13.834
and went straight
to the recording studio,

00:05:13.834 --> 00:05:16.267
which was very crazy.

00:05:16.267 --> 00:05:17.801
And then finished it
the next day on Monday.

00:05:17.801 --> 00:05:19.467
And then it was out
a couple days later.

00:05:19.467 --> 00:05:21.634
So, it was during such
a busy time.

00:05:21.634 --> 00:05:24.534
-Yeah, but even with that,
no one even got to promote it

00:05:24.534 --> 00:05:26.267
or whatever -- it went to
number seven on the chart.

00:05:26.267 --> 00:05:28.133
-It did. I know.
It's just like --

00:05:28.133 --> 00:05:29.567
-That's massive.
-Thank you.

00:05:29.567 --> 00:05:31.300
I know.
For a Broadway record.

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:32.501
It was number one --
-For a Broadway --

00:05:32.501 --> 00:05:34.167
-Yeah, it was number one
on the Broadway charts.

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:36.868
But worldwide, it was like,
Taylor Swift was number one

00:05:36.868 --> 00:05:38.000
and we were number seven.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:41.167
-Yeah, we'll take that.
-I'll take it.

00:05:41.167 --> 00:05:42.801
-I'm always amazed
by your talent,

00:05:42.801 --> 00:05:44.267
and I'm so thankful that you
come to our show.

00:05:44.267 --> 00:05:45.801
-Thank you.
-You are just unbelievable.

00:05:45.801 --> 00:05:47.267
And please, hug that baby
for me.

00:05:47.267 --> 00:05:48.767
-I will.
-Lea Michele, everybody.

00:05:48.767 --> 00:05:49.801
Come on.
-Thank you.

00:05:49.801 --> 00:05:51.300
-"Funny Girl" is
playing at Broadway's

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:52.767
August Wilson Theater.

00:05:52.767 --> 00:05:55.200
You can stream
the new Broadway cast recording

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:57.067
of "Funny Girl" now.

00:05:57.067 --> 00:05:59.968
It will be available on CD
next Friday.

